 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_CWohO9wAdUu5cU9w_28Hzg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:AccruedExpensesAndOtherLiabilitiesCurrent" scale="3" id="Tc_JWMRF21z4U6ctrTbDriNbA_13_2">322,034</ix:nonFraction></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.59%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_YbCFQ_bWu02uoN-a8GX8kw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:AccruedExpensesAndOtherLiabilitiesCurrent" scale="3" id="Tc_74stxKOF8EGIi0WQ_ds2qg_13_4">204,388</ix:nonFraction></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:2.01%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 0pt 0.05pt 0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.87%;border-bottom:3px double #000000;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0.05pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_LY5SbL077UuXzIvTBWGN_g" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_YbCFQ_bWu02uoN-a8GX8kw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:AccruedExpensesAndOtherLiabilitiesCurrent" scale="3" id="Tc_7oroVUCCJkmqpAS_tZlKUg_13_6">29,226</ix:nonFraction></p></td></tr></table><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(a) Deposits from packaged-tour users represent cash paid to the Group as a deposit for overseas tours, and such amount is refundable upon completion of the tours.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(b) Advanced payment from banks represent cash received by the Group for promotional and marketing campaigns. Banks participating in these campaigns would reimburse the Group for tours sold to their credit card holders at a specified discount. Such advanced payment is recognized as revenues when revenues from the related tour are recognized.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;">(c) Discounted bank acceptance notes represent cash received from financial institutions by discounting of bank acceptance notes issued between the Company&#8217;s subsidiaries, which are repayable within one year with interest rate ranging from <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_x2whJFx_u0-eznSq_duWnw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_sn3H7L1i40yrosmMC8YdDg">0.90</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_9FXqzraVakGGqhuDwMY8aQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_-XJ9Wj2eykO6eGieesUztQ">1.25</ix:nonFraction>%. The issuance of notes payable is collateralized by the Group&#8217;s bank deposits of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_us-gaap_InvestmentTypeAxis_us-gaap_ShortTermInvestmentsMember_rQ_d_YJlg0ys9-jqd8dcyA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:DiscountedBankAcceptanceNotesCurrent" scale="3" id="Narr_Ua48KaFjh0KHxC9KX9KMSA">180,000</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_InvestmentTypeAxis_us-gaap_ShortTermInvestmentsMember_7qNifSlKxUy2ncXs9GLH4w" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:DiscountedBankAcceptanceNotesCurrent" scale="3" id="Narr_chLtljJHIkC59UfAsDx5YA">100,000</ix:nonFraction> as of December 31, 2024 and 2025, respectively, which were recorded in short-term investments.</p></ix:nonNumeric></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-38</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">TUNIU CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(All amounts in thousands, except for share and per share data, or otherwise noted)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_WIfOC0S8e0maSoeEnRWSQw" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_iBG6TAaoaUWCF4OgZEa8gQ" continuedAt="Tb_iBG6TAaoaUWCF4OgZEa8gQ_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">14. Income Taxes</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company is registered in the Cayman Islands. The Company generates substantially all of its income (loss) from its PRC operations for the&#160;years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 18pt;">Cayman Islands (&#8220;Cayman&#8221;)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the current laws of the Cayman Islands, the Company is not subject to tax on income or capital gains. Additionally, upon payments of dividends to shareholders, no Cayman Islands withholding tax will be imposed.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 18pt;">Hong Kong</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Entities incorporated in Hong Kong are subject to Hong Kong profits tax at a rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_HK_cQyg0-4HbE2kG4EHx9ZykA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_mDOuwN3Cz02-k9_Ho8W7MQ">16.5</ix:nonFraction>% since January&#160;1, 2010. The operations in Hong Kong have incurred net accumulated operating losses for income tax purposes.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 18pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">PRC</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On March&#160;16, 2007, the National People&#8217;s Congress enacted an Enterprise Income Tax Law (&#8220;EIT Law&#8221;), under which Foreign Investment Enterprises (&#8220;FIEs&#8221;) and domestic companies are subject to EIT at a uniform rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_WIfOC0S8e0maSoeEnRWSQw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_0LHb_4-Q_kCpWK2UXGVTuQ">25</ix:nonFraction>%. The EIT law became effective on January&#160;1, 2008.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The EIT Law and its implementation rules also permit qualified &#8220;high and new technology enterprises,&#8221; or HNTEs, to enjoy a preferential enterprise income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_0it_-H4GxkyN1h5-23NKbw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:IncomeTaxPreferentialTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_qFK-lXsyrEGxO8dO7B-pmQ">15</ix:nonFraction>% upon filing with the tax authorities. The qualification as a HNTE is generally effective for a term of three years and the renewal of such qualification is subject to review by the authorities in China. Nanjing Tuniu originally obtained its HNTE certificate in 2010 with a valid period of three years and successfully obtained the third renewal of such certificate in December 2022 for another three years. Tuniu Nanjing Information Technology obtained its HNTE certificate in 2017 with a valid period of three years and successfully obtained its second renewal of such a certificate in December 2023 for another three years. Therefore, Nanjing Tuniu and Tuniu Nanjing Information Technology are eligible to enjoy a preferential tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_dei_LegalEntityAxis_tour_NanjingTuniuTuniuNanjingInformationTechnologyAndBeijingTuniuMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_ZHwdZlCQHEOPYhFckvbj4Q" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:IncomeTaxPreferentialTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_l-VMiSF9lEaWdbKy7_LVgQ">15</ix:nonFraction>% in 2025 to the extent they have taxable income under the EIT Law, as long as they maintain the HNTE qualifications and duly conduct relevant EIT filing procedures with the relevant tax authorities. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The EIT Law also imposes a withholding income tax of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2008_To_12_31_2008_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_epqn2Q0cCkSzLM9RxxSS8A" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:WithholdingIncomeTaxRateOnDividends" scale="-2" id="Narr_O8mVSVd59kuAFB0hkKGP8Q">10</ix:nonFraction>% on dividends distributed by a FIE to its immediate holding company outside of mainland China, if such immediate holding company is considered as a non-resident enterprise without any establishment or place within mainland China or if the received dividends have no connection with the establishment or place of such immediate holding company within mainland China, unless such immediate holding company&#8217;s jurisdiction of incorporation has a tax treaty with mainland China that provides for a different withholding arrangement. The Cayman Islands, where the Company incorporated, does not have such tax treaty with mainland China. According to the arrangement between mainland China and Hong Kong Special Administrative Region on the Avoidance of Double Taxation and Prevention of Fiscal Evasion in August 2006, dividends paid by a FIE in mainland China to its immediate holding company in Hong Kong will be subject to withholding tax at a rate of no more than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_0it_-H4GxkyN1h5-23NKbw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:MaximumWithholdingTaxRateIfImmediateHoldingHongKongTaxResidentHoldMoreThanSpecificPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_CV0t5rEXdE6OLnHqYdnAlw">5</ix:nonFraction>% if the immediate holding company in Hong Kong owns directly at least <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_CN_0it_-H4GxkyN1h5-23NKbw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:MinimumPercentageOfEquityInterestInPRCResidentEnterpriseToBeHeldByQualifiedHongKongTaxResidentForReducedWithholdingTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_NoJrKSyCzUGFKUpkdR9WLQ">25</ix:nonFraction>% of the shares of the FIE and could be recognized as a Beneficial Owner of the dividend from PRC tax perspective.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-39</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">TUNIU CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(All amounts in thousands, except for share and per share data, or otherwise noted)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="_787df75e_2322_4acf_9c73_b17d579596f5"></a><a id="Tc_rP5C3RW8C0CCHdSqYJ2scQ_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_N72inWgMfUOMueH5YjgfvQ_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_VnlubDKUBEKHqha9Ok7f5A_2_4"></a><a id="Tc_0e4IBjPAC0qAtEP_-hg8tQ_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_54JC2cXbDUmsFmzss723lw_3_4"></a><a id="Tc_lVb3ewVkZkCNl5ed6o2jyg_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_6GdDmGruuU6q1dxJlADuXA_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_WbXbYAKdMEu3Ikcim4_uSQ_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_aQKnm2ES302zi3VqlBJ2qA_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_yMf-t4nQdku2d98jnkDTcQ_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_g-_uOZr1n0au0wZn6a_YWA_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_otZhKgQsikeBahS5cUEqeg_10_0"></a><a id="_908bcf35_7cc7_4eb9_af57_dcf0ff7b8748"></a><a id="Tc_LbWRyQ4YGU-XZiI68W1e3w_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_hex2MEsDUUyZpejOAWklWQ_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_WIsVO7Pm-USfrtjFH9z68Q_3_2"></a><a i