<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">TUNIU CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(All amounts in thousands, except for share and per share data, or otherwise noted)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_isU--24ZOk29fYfzpLktAg_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_isU--24ZOk29fYfzpLktAg_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">21. Related party transactions and balances - continued</b></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">a)</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Transactions with related parties:</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:12pt;"></div><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 18pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Trip.com</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Trip.com purchased <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2014_To_12_31_2014_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_tour_PrivatePlacementConcurrentWithIPOMember_NzzCKI5iIEWnWQe5VxejaA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_vX_LyidWakKFaYPzgsi7LA">5,000,000</ix:nonFraction> Class&#160;A ordinary shares in a private placement concurrent with the Company&#8217;s initial public offering, an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2014_To_12_31_2014_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_PrivatePlacementMember_6vJiRwPfs0WbRzDfFkAvbw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_oQ9cjcYmDEmh4PwA0-IYyg">3,731,034</ix:nonFraction> Class&#160;A ordinary shares for a total of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_LY5SbL077UuXzIvTBWGN_g" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2014_To_12_31_2014_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_PrivatePlacementMember_6vJiRwPfs0WbRzDfFkAvbw" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfCommonStock" scale="6" id="Narr_tipjL9EhY024qtnxKihazA">15</ix:nonFraction> million through a private placement transaction in December&#160;2014 as well as an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_5_1_2015_To_5_31_2015_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_PrivatePlacementMember_ORKUteSQ2E6syu1jH5SoYA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_Z-0Wz4oCBEKXZXqOjOQjCg">3,750,000</ix:nonFraction> Class&#160;A ordinary shares for a total of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_LY5SbL077UuXzIvTBWGN_g" contextRef="Duration_5_1_2015_To_5_31_2015_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_PrivatePlacementMember_ORKUteSQ2E6syu1jH5SoYA" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfCommonStock" scale="6" id="Narr_NvmQCFWWykSurJdNfjO6XQ">20</ix:nonFraction> million through a private placement transaction in May&#160;2015.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group sells packaged tours through Trip.com&#8217;s online platform and the commission fees to Trip.com were insignificant. The Group purchased travel products from Trip.com&#8217;s online platform, which were insignificant. Gross proceeds from Trip.com consist of commission fees for the booking of hotel rooms and air tickets through the Group&#8217;s online platform, amounted of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_2RtZMCRnnkS6Wd3EGbUPjw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_6AyTV-soZUSWd_YZTi644w">nil</ix:nonFraction>, RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_WKlhVFlmaUe4FaZLQ51GRA" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_IhEF_InfHka-ooEGcxwzdA">111.3</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CtripMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_yEQI36T1oEWXSSfXq8-KiQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_UPHn0f_QyECoDg-uaoML-Q">5.1</ix:nonFraction> for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">JD</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On May 8, 2015, the Company issued <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_5_8_2015_To_5_8_2015_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_FabulousJadeGlobalLimitedMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_cwPhiHlOD0OniFcynUziSA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_STGDNE1fXEqRl9FeyRky5Q">65,625,000</ix:nonFraction> Class A ordinary shares to Fabulous Jade Global Limited, a subsidiary of JD, for cash consideration of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_5_8_2015_To_5_8_2015_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_FabulousJadeGlobalLimitedMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_cwPhiHlOD0OniFcynUziSA" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfCommonStock" scale="6" id="Narr_jYszyWvRvU299sFqY8y5Lw">1,528.2</ix:nonFraction> million and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_5_8_2015_To_5_8_2015_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_FabulousJadeGlobalLimitedMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_cwPhiHlOD0OniFcynUziSA" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodValueNewIssues" scale="6" id="Narr_Xc1tacUPpUa4M2wtv1hrIA">660.2</ix:nonFraction> million representing the fair value of business resource contributed by JD.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On November 20, 2020, JD completed transfer of all its equity interest in the Group to Caissa. Subsequently on February 9, 2021, Caissa assigned a director to the Company&#8217;s board of directors to replace the director previously assigned by JD and since then, JD was no longer a related party of the Group. In December 2023, JD.com E-commerce (Investment) Hong Kong Corporation Limited, JD, Caissa, Caissa Sega Tourism Culture Development Group Co., Ltd. and Fabulous Jade Global Limited entered into a termination agreement, pursuant to which the parties agreed to terminate the share purchase agreement and agreed for the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_JdcomInvestmentLimitedMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_bZDzAV9CGkWlenUJ37lr4w" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:NumberOfSharesToBeTransferredOnTerminationOfSharePurchaseAgreement" scale="0" id="Narr__5QJy1BorEiQjxUf0gBgvg">78,061,780</ix:nonFraction> Class A ordinary shares then beneficially owned by Caissa and Fabulous Jade Global Limited to be returned and transferred to JD. Subsequently on February 29, 2024, JD assigned a director to the Company&#8217;s board of directors to replace the director previously assigned by Caissa and since then, JD became a related party of the Group.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group paid JD a commission of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_JdcomInvestmentLimitedMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_84EZ7fsqTE-HG7Dkumtepw" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:PaymentOfCommissionForSellingProducts" scale="3" id="Narr_Zm31ukPrTESJZRy56JKZpQ">38.5</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_JdcomInvestmentLimitedMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_WpF8cio-x0G1W0cxJHTLMQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:PaymentOfCommissionForSellingProducts" scale="3" id="Narr_9vt11J5a2U64Pe3FBIIX_A">106.9</ix:nonFraction> for selling products on the JD platform for the years ended December 31, 2024 and 2025, respectively. Gross proceeds from JD consist of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_JdcomInvestmentLimitedMember_srt_ProductOrServiceAxis_tour_TravelServicesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_3VTcLNi2rk2xd5kW-IFcVw" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_xT6w3U5EiE6AcpslzgcIkg">1,164.4</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_JdcomInvestmentLimitedMember_srt_ProductOrServiceAxis_tour_TravelServicesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_TQIIiOhBIUWpUhHezeo5sQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_MdlPO5Yiu0yF0N-XDZ_vEA">1,633.5</ix:nonFraction> for providing business travel services and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_JdcomInvestmentLimitedMember_srt_ProductOrServiceAxis_tour_TeamBuildingServicesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_TZgmyra3YU-PBJZRB4IAaA" decimals="-1" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_RI6RPBBs_0202ibT9A5J9g">151.0</ix:nonFraction> and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_JdcomInvestmentLimitedMember_srt_ProductOrServiceAxis_tour_TeamBuildingServicesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_0IcYiL4dGU2YIxxm-bRuNQ" decimals="1" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_RbFm4iHe8kqsbn5J4TMnig">nil</ix:nonFraction> for team-building services for the years ended December 31, 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Caissa</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On November 20, 2020, pursuant to a share purchase agreement and certain amendments, Caissa completed the purchase of all Class A ordinary shares of the Company from JD and became a related party of the Group. Subsequently on February 9, 2021, Caissa assigned a director to the Company&#8217;s board of directors to replace the director previously assigned by JD. In December 2023, JD.com E-commerce (Investment) Hong Kong Corporation Limited, JD, Caissa, Caissa Sega Tourism Culture Development Group Co., Ltd. and Fabulous Jade Global Limited entered into a termination agreement, pursuant to which the parties agreed to terminate the share purchase agreement and agreed for the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CaissaMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_37wi_g_KbUqO9LnNQov6cQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:NumberOfSharesToBeTransferredOnTerminationOfSharePurchaseAgreement" scale="0" id="Narr_vZKWqz0_VUi4HY0kemofkQ">78,061,780</ix:nonFraction> Class A ordinary shares then beneficially owned by Caissa and Fabulous Jade Global Limited to be returned and transferred to JD. Subsequently on February 29, 2024, JD assigned a director to the Company&#8217;s board of directors to replace the director previously assigned by Caissa and since then, Caissa was no longer a related party of the Group.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During the year ended December 31, 2023, the Group received cash of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CaissaMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_37wi_g_KbUqO9LnNQov6cQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LoansAndLeasesReceivableRelatedPartiesProceeds" scale="3" id="Narr_HPjDKeWb_EO_0u84DYfy-Q">332.4</ix:nonFraction> and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CaissaMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_37wi_g_KbUqO9LnNQov6cQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:NumberOfSharesReceivedForCollectionOfLoansToRelatedParties" scale="0" id="Narr_yC_iam7TN0CBet_lvdGfjQ">311,075</ix:nonFraction> shares of Caissa Tosun Development Co., Ltd. (listed on the Shenzhen Stock Exchange) with value of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CaissaMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_37wi_g_KbUqO9LnNQov6cQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:ValueOfSharesReceivedForCollectionOfLoansToRelatedParties" scale="3" id="Narr_IzpuWwT-bkmveJ_8pWRBkA">1,235.0</ix:nonFraction> as part of the settlement of the Caissa debts, of which CECL allowance was fully provided in the prior years. Accordingly, a reversal of CECL allowance at the amount of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_CaissaMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_37wi_g_KbUqO9LnNQov6cQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProvisionForLoanLossesExpensed" scale="3" id="Narr_D5X1hXzRUEmwt5CvO_7Siw">1,567.4</ix:nonFraction> was credited to the consolidated statements of comprehensive loss in 2023.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-48</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">TUNIU CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(All amounts in thousands, except for share and per share data, or otherwise noted)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_isU--24ZOk29fYfzpLktAg_cont2" continuedAt="Tb_isU--24ZOk29fYfzpLktAg_cont3"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">21. Related party transactions and balances - continued</b></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="width:18pt;"/><td style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">a)</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Transactions with related parties (continued):</span></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:12pt;"></div><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">HNA Tourism and HNA Trust</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On January 21, 2016, the Company issued <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2016_To_1_21_2016_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_sseTgD9YtkO7PRhc5NxdKA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_L3mRiKd_G0OM-0bLXBY9LQ">90,909,091</ix:nonFraction> Class A ordinary shares to HNA Tourism Holdings Group Co., Ltd. (&#8220;HNA Tourism&#8221;) for total consideration of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_21_2016_To_1_21_2016_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_sseTgD9YtkO7PRhc5NxdKA" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromIssuanceOfCommonStock" scale="6" id="Narr_JZybbkEij0WUFeItw58GyQ">3,279</ix:nonFraction> million. Before restructuring of HNA Group, certain affiliates of HNA Tourism agreed to provide the Group with access to its premium airlines and hotels resources at a preferential rate, under fair competition market rules. After the restructuring of HNA Group, these affiliates of HNA Tourism were no longer the Group&#8217;s related parties.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Before 2021, the Group provided financing to certain affiliates of HNA Tourism (the &#8220;HNA Affiliates&#8221;) with total principal amount of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2020_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_H8Y2g7K-nUiY-ZnlgzgAhg" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:NotesAndLoansReceivableNetCurrent" scale="6" id="Narr_73Hc3YnC2E20FNvMnSnb1g">540</ix:nonFraction> million and full allowance for CECL was provided for receivables due from HNA Affiliates (&#8220;HNA debts&#8221;).</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In January 2021, HNA Group received a formal bankruptcy and restructuring notice from the Hainan Province High People&#8217;s Court (the &#8220;Court&#8221;) following creditors&#8217; action against HNA Group due to its failure to pay overdue debts. In October 2021, debt restructuring plans of HNA Group and its affiliates were approved by the creditors and the Court, pursuant to which HNA Group and its affiliates would settle their debts owed to the creditors by various means, including cash, shares of Hainan Airlines Holding Co., Ltd., (&#8220;HNA Airlines&#8221;), a company listed in Chinese A share market, and units in a trust (&#8220;HNA Trust&#8221;) comprising assets/liabilities of HNA Group and certain of its affiliates, etc. In December 2021, the Group received cash of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_4WaUFpv-t0W01SFg2GTJjw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LoansAndLeasesReceivableRelatedPartiesProceeds" scale="6" id="Narr_-aun1HPA9EmnE2CGqXBwLA">0.3</ix:nonFraction> million and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_4WaUFpv-t0W01SFg2GTJjw" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:NumberOfSharesReceivedForCollectionOfLoansToRelatedParties" scale="0" id="Narr_O1nYAxz79Ue5Oo34iLcmKQ">531,591</ix:nonFraction> shares of HNA Airlines with value of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_4WaUFpv-t0W01SFg2GTJjw" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:ValueOfSharesReceivedForCollectionOfLoansToRelatedParties" scale="6" id="Narr_YbZcXrD_vkaXIYCV9igVVA">1</ix:nonFraction> million as part of the settlement of the HNA debts, of which CECL allowance was fully provided in the prior years. Accordingly, a reversal of CECL allowance at the amount of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2021_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_E37kWs-GEE-syX496dMJmQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:RelatedPartyTransactionAllowanceForCreditLoss" scale="6" id="Narr_xw4iiPAZZECdLM_0w6SKAA">1.3</ix:nonFraction> million was credited to the consolidated statements of comprehensive loss in 2021.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">For the year ended December 31, 2022, the Group received additional cash of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2022_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaAffiliatesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_tour_NotesFinancingAndLoanFinancingMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember__bwIEMLj-kmgB8GmCuWLUA" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Cash" scale="3" id="Narr_Lg197O_jfE6LC-dglSdo6g">150</ix:nonFraction> and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaAffiliatesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_tour_NotesFinancingAndLoanFinancingMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_coad2DJCqUyXHSIChG21lg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_tSA_v5QMAkCWcH2atqOn-w">2,398</ix:nonFraction> shares of HNA Airlines with value of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaAffiliatesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_tour_NotesFinancingAndLoanFinancingMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_yjkV0kG58EqI6FVojqJZlg" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProvisionForLoanLossesExpensed" scale="3" id="Narr_ajRyZYSHq06YWBUvTMvhLw">3.9</ix:nonFraction> as part of the settlement of the HNA debts, of which CECL allowance was fully provided in the prior years. Accordingly, a reversal of CECL allowance at the amount of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaAffiliatesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_tour_NotesFinancingMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_8cxgZfIwOUSyTkpTgvdmow" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProvisionForLoanLossesExpensed" scale="3" id="Narr_ISGKOUHWKk6lHgbH66vrLw">153.9</ix:nonFraction> was credited to the consolidated statements of comprehensive loss in 2022. In April 2022, as confirmed by the Court, the restructuring plan has been fully implemented and HNA Trust was officially established. In May 2022, the Company received and registered <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_aEx_wvfvxEWJi6J1VcvYRQ" contextRef="Duration_5_1_2022_To_5_31_2022_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_YA4-xRZqg0qxJa1m0w9UPA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:NumberOfUnitsReceivedAndRegisteredForSettlementOfDebts" scale="0" id="Narr_fMcQM-btXUWwZ50Vxa1azw">632,992,650</ix:nonFraction> trust units (representing <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_HWvhQR0-ukSb-U3gHiU3bg" contextRef="Duration_5_1_2022_To_5_31_2022_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_YA4-xRZqg0qxJa1m0w9UPA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:PercentageOfUnitsReceivedForSettlementOfDebts" scale="-2" id="Narr_uIeRqlYSmUSNRM1eLwjDPw">0.09</ix:nonFraction>% of unit interests of HNA trust) with the value of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTourismHoldingsGroupCoLtdMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_W9ksS4NxE0-mitnQmLx-Qw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:InitialInvestmentOnReceiptOfUnits" scale="6" id="Narr_w3s194oYyUi5f6Sh8bMVqg">13.3</ix:nonFraction> million, as the settlement of remaining HNA debts. The Group recognized the trust units as equity investment without readily determinable fair value and derecognized all the remaining HNA debts which was fully provided (refer to Note 6 for details of accounting treatment of the trust units), meanwhile a corresponding reversal of CECL allowance with the amount of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaAffiliatesMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_-8oKGmjWDkW4BwLyh0NNOA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="tour:ValueOfSharesReceivedForCollectionOfLoansToRelatedParties" scale="6" id="Narr_7LycRAzyU0-yoZOob7_wvw">13.3</ix:nonFraction> million was credited to the consolidated statements of comprehensive loss for the year ended December 31, 2022.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group received cash of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTrustMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_8YCYPcK1RUmFAbrzyAZPJg" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromDividendsReceived" scale="3" id="Narr_7On4p-MMNk2sjGp9AGNYMQ">211.8</ix:nonFraction>, RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTrustMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_tour_NotesFinancingMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_UIFHjE8AiEmzAVnL_RqgLg" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromDividendsReceived" scale="3" id="Narr_69snKmVj30ibi2EqzTwWog">211.3</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HnaTrustMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_f4gseUhekE6gHzqYDSaa7Q" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromDividendsReceived" scale="3" id="Narr_sHeEeMcuAE2JsfqfyE-TVQ">351.8</ix:nonFraction> from HNA Trust with the equivalent trust units deregistered according to the trust agreement for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Hengxin</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group purchased travel products from Hengxin, amounted to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HengxinMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_VCNv9ZUI4Ua-yzqEOkH4qQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionPurchasesFromRelatedParty" scale="3" id="Narr_dM4l7mcM4kuDv6-WPsHekA">2,729.3</ix:nonFraction>, RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HengxinMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_Qd0L9U6wSkWslpUEEE8aTw" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionPurchasesFromRelatedParty" scale="3" id="Narr_T_yI7_cHfESvtP7xXy8xmA">7,888.6</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HengxinMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_Dc8QDeRfOkKhMLf3fMhA2Q" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionPurchasesFromRelatedParty" scale="3" id="Narr_qNDWU-06hkeeNrNIZkKMWA">10,667.1</ix:nonFraction> for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025, respectively. The Group disposed the controlling interest in Hengxin in June 2022 and confirmed with Hengxin an outstanding loan amounted to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HengxinMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_Wx6sJSWAIEymJ85KDXqlsw" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherLiabilities" scale="3" id="Narr_EYVrBmtglkyJ6iLgr8gssg">11,258.6</ix:nonFraction>. The Group received loan repayment of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_HengxinMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_Dc8QDeRfOkKhMLf3fMhA2Q" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromCollectionOfLongtermLoansToRelatedParties" scale="3" id="Narr_B_4bL4F2mUehbZtVjCfjcw">2,000.0</ix:nonFraction> for the year ended December 31, 2025.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Yijianyou</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group purchased travel products from Yijianyou, amounted to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_GuangxiYijianyouTourismOperationCoLtdYijianyouMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_Fb7fMYBmO0uwCHlHebcsFQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionPurchasesFromRelatedParty" scale="3" id="Narr_CI7cSnkMZ06kj0zbUOceOA">nil</ix:nonFraction>, RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_GuangxiYijianyouTourismOperationCoLtdYijianyouMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_L2BJ_mYdsk2NeRcp0u0SOA" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionPurchasesFromRelatedParty" scale="3" id="Narr_hLSMREGxMUmLCk6KyokFtQ">890.5</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_GuangxiYijianyouTourismOperationCoLtdYijianyouMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_4T3cKjQwCEKtSPx4RqpObg" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionPurchasesFromRelatedParty" scale="3" id="Narr_EwawOSbMYkWsVhjWd2P9gw">494.8</ix:nonFraction> for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025, respectively. Gross proceeds from Yijianyou consist of commission fees for promoting travel products by live streaming, amounted to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_GuangxiYijianyouTourismOperationCoLtdYijianyouMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_Fb7fMYBmO0uwCHlHebcsFQ" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_bpv2MfMMcU2IP_NftqAXrA">28.0</ix:nonFraction>, RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_GuangxiYijianyouTourismOperationCoLtdYijianyouMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_L2BJ_mYdsk2NeRcp0u0SOA" decimals="-2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_tunMC206H0-sQCmLb0KCSw">352.3</ix:nonFraction> and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_KLlvWlT6dE2YYlR3I7zG2A" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_tour_GuangxiYijianyouTourismOperationCoLtdYijianyouMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_4T3cKjQwCEKtSPx4RqpObg" decimals="-2" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax" scale="3" id="Narr_wnj8DGqN0kKLkldoaEyCCA">nil</ix:nonFraction> for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024, and 2025, respectively.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-49</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">TUNIU CORPORATION</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(All amounts in thousands, except for share and per share data, or otherwise noted)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><a id="Tc_efqxDoT2WUu3gyWXZsjxng_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_jOgLL3e4w0OJQCO_kTUH-Q_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_dcDnktA5U0ehT9KDe7LhFQ_2_4"></a><a id="Tc_qtRwz2HcKki7eFtbENI8tg_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_RzLpRVEcBEi7w3CttkQI5g_3_4"></a><a id="Tc_iQAlzWPJr0u9vPJExK6nSg_3_6"></a><a id="Tc_r98KrA4abk-HYZg05hPfoQ_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_s5LoZoQ770qkVtZxay8K8g_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_-WOK0k8PB06nvdqXfJcB8A_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_a4SBCcQew0KRD5DXMyikOA_6_2"></a><a id="Tc_6Hdt4x-wpkm2YkwgYao_Dg_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_sFgF-HcESEyAniEUqQEKxw_8_0"></a><a id="Tc_ba3wON7nJkOEmOWr74IHvw_9_0"></a><a id="Tc_O3BBcxwmtEygjU5app3ufw_10_0"></a><a id="Tc__3yUnywZgEewmCQHMbsYKA_12_0"></a><a id="Tc__r5TaHn3GUeaAinjs8OEnw_13_0"></a><a id="Tc_EXv5gY8H-0aBbjVBG08AZA_14_0"></a><a id="Tc_hThpt-A